# A8.3 — DOES A PART READ AS A DOOR, WITH NOTHING BUT CELLS IN IT?
#
# `door.keys` asks the same question of the editor's own wall-opening gesture. This
# asks it of a PART: `door/hung`, a wall with a one-hex doorway and a leaf hung in
# it, opened in part mode and photographed from where a person would stand.
#
#   node tools/script.mjs tools/scripts/doorway.keys --port <p> --shots
#
# ⚠ PART MODE IS THE ONLY PLACE THIS PICTURE EXISTS. `14:<roof>,<part>` in a WORLD
# stamps the named part's own cells and expands nothing — no instance, no limb — so
# a doorway placed that way is its paving and nothing else. `44:` swaps the store
# and the display world IS the expansion, which is what puts the wall and the leaf
# in one picture.
#
# ⚠ CLOSE BEFORE OPENING. A server keeps its mode between runs and `44:<name>`
# refuses while a part is already open — the previous run's picture came back under
# the new name's script, with no error anyone read.
#
# ⚠ AND THE CAMERA HAS TO BE PLACED AFTER THE SWAP, because the part is a few hexes
# across at the origin and the author stands where the world left them.

send 44:
at 0 0 0
verb raise
wait rebuilt

echo --- open the doorway as a part
send 44:door/hung
wait part 'door/hung' opened

# ⚠ AUTO, NOT EYES. A limb's mesh id is 8..15 and the client's `mesh_bit` answers
# `1` — the FIGURE's bit — for every id at or below 15, so EYES hides the leaf along
# with the body. The obvious way to get the walker out of the picture is the one way
# that cannot photograph this subject.
send 40:0
wait mode

# ⚠ THE STATIONS ARE CHOSEN FOR THE LEAF'S PLANE, NOT FOR THE WALL'S. Ajar by an
# eighth of a turn the leaf stands 45° out of the wall, which is nearly EDGE-ON from
# due south — the first three shots of this doorway were taken from there and read
# as an empty opening. The west station is the one that sees its face.
echo --- from the west, where an ajar leaf shows its face
at -4.9 -1.3 15
snap a83-door-w

echo --- from the south-west, the wall and the leaf together
at -3.0 -4.0 40
snap a83-door-sw

echo --- and square on to the wall, where the opening reads
at 0.0 -5.5 70
snap a83-door-s

echo --- back to the world, so nothing is left open
send 44:
